  "final_answer": "If the backend endpoint `GET /api/admin/featuresInfo` is deleted, this change is **BREAKING** for the Angular frontend. \n\nThe following TypeScript consumers and UI components will be broken:\n\n### 1. **Service Layer**\n* **File:** `ui-ngx/src/app/core/http/admin.service.ts`\n* **Affected Member:** `getFeaturesInfo(config?: RequestConfig): Observable<FeaturesInfo>`\n* **Description:** This method makes a direct HTTP `GET` call to `/api/admin/featuresInfo`. If the endpoint is deleted, calling this method will result in an HTTP error (e.g., 404 Not Found).\n  ```typescript\n  public getFeaturesInfo(config?: RequestConfig): Observable<FeaturesInfo> {\n    return this.http.get<FeaturesInfo>('/api/admin/featuresInfo', defaultHttpOptionsFromConfig(config));\n  }\n  ```\n\n### 2. **Component Layer**\n* **File:** `ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/components/widget/lib/home-page/configured-features.component.ts`\n* **Affected Member:** `ConfiguredFeaturesComponent` (specifically in `ngOnInit`)\n* **Description:** Under the System Administrator (`SYS_ADMIN`) authority, this component fetches the configuration status of features to populate the **\"Configured Features\"** home page/dashboard widget:\n  ```typescript\n  (this.authUser.authority === Authority.SYS_ADMIN ?\n  this.adminService.getFeaturesInfo() : of(null)).subscribe(\n    (featuresInfo) => {\n      this.featuresInfo = featuresInfo;\n      this.cd.markForCheck();\n    }\n  );\n  ```\n\n### 3. **Template Layer**\n* **File:** `ui-ngx/src/app/modules/home/components/widget/lib/home-page/configured-features.component.html`\n* **Description:** The UI template uses `featuresInfo` properties to conditionally show visual elements, check/close icons, and set status classes for key features:\n  * White Labeling (`featuresInfo?.whiteLabelingEnabled`)\n  * Outgoing Mail/Email (`featuresInfo?.emailEnabled`)\n  *",
